:: Q2
Which shorthand notation corresponds to palmitic acid?
<<checkbox "$q2_A" false true>> A. C18:0
<<checkbox "$q2_B" false true>> B. C14:0
<<checkbox "$q2_C" false true>> C. C16:0
<<checkbox "$q2_D" false true>> D. C16:1(9Z)
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F2">><</button>>

:: F2
<<set _correct=0>><<set _incorrect=0>><<set _missed=[]>><<set _wrong=[]>>
<<if $q2_C>><<set _correct +=1>><<else>><<run _missed.push("C. C16:0")>><</if>>
<<if $q2_A>><<set _incorrect +=1>><<run _wrong.push("A. C18:0")>><</if>><<if $q2_B>><<set _incorrect +=1>><<run _wrong.push("B. C14:0")>><</if>><<if $q2_D>><<set _incorrect +=1>><<run _wrong.push("D. C16:1(9Z)")>><</if>>
<<set $totalCorrect += _correct>><<set $totalPossible += 1>><<set $totalIncorrect += _incorrect>>
Model answer: C. C16:0.
Palmitic acid contains sixteen carbon atoms and no double bonds, giving the notation C16:0. C18:0 is stearic acid, C14:0 is myristic acid, and C16:1(9Z) is a monounsaturated fatty acid. Fatty acid nomenclature summarises chain length and degree of unsaturation, features that strongly influence membrane properties, storage lipids, and metabolic processing.
