[[Next->Q3]]

:: Q3
Which property is characteristic of cis double bonds in fatty acids?
<<checkbox "$q3_A" false true>> A. They introduce a bend in the hydrocarbon chain
<<checkbox "$q3_B" false true>> B. They increase chain length
<<checkbox "$q3_C" false true>> C. They remove the carboxyl group
<<checkbox "$q3_D" false true>> D. They make the fatty acid fully saturated
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F3">><</button>>

:: F3
<<set _correct=0>><<set _incorrect=0>><<set _missed=[]>><<set _wrong=[]>><<if $q3_A>><<set _correct+=1>><<else>><<run _missed.push("A. They introduce a bend in the hydrocarbon chain")>><</if>><<if $q3_B>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("B. They increase chain length")>><</if>><<if $q3_C>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("C. They remove the carboxyl group")>><</if>><<if $q3_D>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("D. They make the fatty acid fully saturated")>><</if>><<set $totalCorrect += _correct>><<set $totalPossible += 1>><<set $totalIncorrect += _incorrect>>
Model answer: A. They introduce a bend in the hydrocarbon chain.
Cis double bonds generate kinks that reduce tight packing of fatty acyl chains and increase membrane fluidity. They do not change chain length, remove functional groups, or create saturated fatty acids. Unsaturation affects membrane behaviour, lipid melting temperatures, and interactions of biological membranes with proteins.
