[[Next->Q4]]

:: Q4
Which of the following are products of the pentose phosphate pathway?
<<checkbox "$q4_A" false true>> A. NADPH
<<checkbox "$q4_B" false true>> B. Ribose-5-phosphate
<<checkbox "$q4_C" false true>> C. Acetyl-CoA
<<checkbox "$q4_D" false true>> D. FADH2
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F4">><</button>>

:: F4
<<set _correct=0>><<set _incorrect=0>><<set _missed=[]>><<set _wrong=[]>>
<<if $q4_A>><<set _correct+=1>><<else>><<run _missed.push("A. NADPH")>><</if>><<if $q4_B>><<set _correct+=1>><<else>><<run _missed.push("B. Ribose-5-phosphate")>><</if>><<if $q4_C>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("C. Acetyl-CoA")>><</if>><<if $q4_D>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("D. FADH2")>><</if>><<set $totalCorrect += _correct>><<set $totalPossible += 2>><<set $totalIncorrect += _incorrect>>
Model answer: A. NADPH; B. Ribose-5-phosphate.
The pentose phosphate pathway generates NADPH for reductive biosynthesis and antioxidant defence, and ribose-5-phosphate for nucleotide synthesis. It does not directly produce acetyl-CoA or FADH2. Its oxidative branch supplies reducing power, whereas non-oxidative reactions interconvert sugar phosphates according to cellular biosynthetic demands.
