[[Next->Q5]]

:: Q5
Which are TAGs composed of?
<<checkbox "$q5_A" false true>> A. A glycerol backbone and three fatty acids
<<checkbox "$q5_B" false true>> B. A sphingosine backbone and one fatty acid
<<checkbox "$q5_C" false true>> C. Cholesterol and three fatty acids
<<checkbox "$q5_D" false true>> D. Two glycerol molecules and three fatty acids
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F5">><</button>>

:: F5
<<set _correct=($q5_A?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=0>><<set _missed=[]>><<set _wrong=[]>><<if !$q5_A>><<run _missed.push("A. A glycerol backbone and three fatty acids")>><</if>><<if $q5_B>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("B. A sphingosine backbone and one fatty acid")>><</if>><<if $q5_C>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("C. Cholesterol and three fatty acids")>><</if>><<if $q5_D>><<set _incorrect+=1>><<run _wrong.push("D. Two glycerol molecules and three fatty acids")>><</if>><<set $totalCorrect += _correct>><<set $totalPossible += 1>><<set $totalIncorrect += _incorrect>>
Model answer: A. A glycerol backbone and three fatty acids.
Triacylglycerols contain three fatty acids esterified to a single glycerol molecule and serve as major energy-storage lipids. Sphingosine-containing molecules belong to sphingolipid classes, cholesterol is a sterol, and two glycerol backbones are not part of TAG structure. TAG hydrolysis releases fatty acids for mitochondrial beta-oxidation.
