[[Next->Q6]]

:: Q6
What is the primary role of NADPH in the cell?
<<checkbox "$q6_A" false true>> A. Driving ATP synthesis through the respiratory chain
<<checkbox "$q6_B" false true>> B. Supporting anabolic reactions and antioxidant defence
<<checkbox "$q6_C" false true>> C. Activating fatty acids for beta-oxidation
<<checkbox "$q6_D" false true>> D. Transporting fatty acids into mitochondria
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F6">><</button>>

:: F6
<<set _correct=($q6_B?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=($q6_A?1:0)+($q6_C?1:0)+($q6_D?1:0)>><<set $totalCorrect+=_correct>><<set $totalPossible+=1>><<set $totalIncorrect+=_incorrect>>
Model answer: B. Supporting anabolic reactions and antioxidant defence.
NADPH supplies reducing equivalents for fatty acid and cholesterol synthesis and maintains reduced glutathione for protection against oxidative stress. ATP synthesis primarily depends on NADH oxidation in the respiratory chain. Fatty acid activation requires acyl-CoA synthetases, while mitochondrial transport depends on the carnitine shuttle.
