[[Next->Q7]]

:: Q7
Which process occurs in the mitochondria?
<<checkbox "$q7_A" false true>> A. Fatty acid synthesis
<<checkbox "$q7_B" false true>> B. Pentose phosphate pathway
<<checkbox "$q7_C" false true>> C. Beta-oxidation of fatty acids
<<checkbox "$q7_D" false true>> D. Conversion of citrate to malonyl-CoA
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F7">><</button>>

:: F7
<<set _correct=($q7_C?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=($q7_A?1:0)+($q7_B?1:0)+($q7_D?1:0)>><<set $totalCorrect+=_correct>><<set $totalPossible+=1>><<set $totalIncorrect+=_incorrect>>
Model answer: C. Beta-oxidation of fatty acids.
Beta-oxidation occurs mainly in mitochondria, where fatty acyl chains are degraded to acetyl-CoA, NADH, and FADH2. Fatty acid synthesis and malonyl-CoA formation are cytosolic processes, and the pentose phosphate pathway occurs in the cytosol. Mitochondrial beta-oxidation is central to energy production during fasting.
