[[Next->Q8]]

:: Q8
Which are important features of fatty acid synthesis?
<<checkbox "$q8_A" false true>> A. It occurs in the cytosol
<<checkbox "$q8_B" false true>> B. It requires NADPH
<<checkbox "$q8_C" false true>> C. It occurs only in the nucleus
<<checkbox "$q8_D" false true>> D. It directly generates large amounts of ATP
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F8">><</button>>

:: F8
<<set _correct=($q8_A?1:0)+($q8_B?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=($q8_C?1:0)+($q8_D?1:0)>><<set $totalCorrect+=_correct>><<set $totalPossible+=2>><<set $totalIncorrect+=_incorrect>>
Model answer: A. It occurs in the cytosol; B. It requires NADPH.
Fatty acid synthesis in animal cells occurs in the cytosol and consumes NADPH during reductive elongation reactions catalysed by fatty acid synthase. It is not restricted to the nucleus and does not directly produce ATP. Instead, it uses cellular energy and reducing power to build long-chain fatty acids.
You correctly identified _correct of 2 correct answers. Missed <<=2-_correct>> correct answers. Selected _incorrect incorrect answers.
[[Next->Q9]]

:: Q9
During fatty acid synthesis, which molecule serves as the dedicated carbon donor for chain elongation?
<<checkbox "$q9_A" false true>> A. Citrate
<<checkbox "$q9_B" false true>> B. Acetyl-CoA
<<checkbox "$q9_C" false true>> C. Ribose-5-phosphate
<<checkbox "$q9_D" false true>> D. Malonyl-CoA
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F9">><</button>>

:: F9
<<set _correct=($q9_D?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=($q9_A?1:0)+($q9_B?1:0)+($q9_C?1:0)>><<set $totalCorrect+=_correct>><<set $totalPossible+=1>><<set $totalIncorrect+=_incorrect>>
Model answer: D. Malonyl-CoA.
Malonyl-CoA is the activated two-carbon donor used repeatedly for fatty acid chain elongation. Although acetyl-CoA provides the initial primer and citrate exports carbon from mitochondria, neither functions as the dedicated elongation substrate. Ribose-5-phosphate is involved in nucleotide metabolism rather than lipid biosynthesis.
