[[Next->Q10]]

:: Q10
A lipid identified as PC(16:0/18:1(9Z)) belongs to which class?
<<checkbox "$q10_A" false true>> A. Triacylglycerols
<<checkbox "$q10_B" false true>> B. Glycerophospholipids
<<checkbox "$q10_C" false true>> C. Sphingomyelins
<<checkbox "$q10_D" false true>> D. Steroid hormones
<<button "Submit">><<goto "F10">><</button>>

:: F10
<<set _correct=($q10_B?1:0)>><<set _incorrect=($q10_A?1:0)+($q10_C?1:0)+($q10_D?1:0)>><<set $totalCorrect+=_correct>><<set $totalPossible+=1>><<set $totalIncorrect+=_incorrect>>
Model answer: B. Glycerophospholipids.
The abbreviation PC denotes phosphatidylcholine, a glycerophospholipid containing a glycerol backbone, phosphate group, choline head group, and specified fatty acyl chains. Triacylglycerols are storage lipids, sphingomyelins contain sphingosine, and steroid hormones derive from sterol structures. Glycerophospholipids are major components of biological membranes.
